From ca78703f88dcac97f19ba8f3a6d1d1c3713c70ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Wylie <wylieb@google.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:39:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-121133: Incorrect reference resolution in
 Images

Cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8592985:
Do not follow symlinks in ImageDataStoreDisk

ImageDataStoreDisk reads and writes cache entries with
base::ReadFileToString and base::WriteFile, which follow symlinks. On
Mac, the image cache lives in a directory a less privileged process can
also write to, so a symlink planted there makes the browser process
read or overwrite files outside the cache.

Reject symlinked storage directories and open cache entries with
File::FLAG_NO_FOLLOW, which turns a planted symlink into a cache miss
or a failed write.

Fixed: 574604188
